<title>USA: Cooper Cos Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Cooper Cos Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>PLEASANTON, Calif 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.40		    $0.24</p>
<p> Net		 4,669		    2,820</p>
<p> Revs		28,871		   25,249</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  11,793		   11,589</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.69		    $0.32</p>
<p> Net		 8,130		    3,700</p>
<p> Revs		77,895		   72,253</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  11,741		   11,580</p>
<p>(All data above 000s)</p>
<p>NOTE - Results for 1996 third quarter include a gain of $615,000, or $0.05 per share, related to the reversal of tax accruals no longer required, but not related to anticipated recording of deferred tax assets in the 1996 fourth quarter.</p>
<p>Full company name is The Cooper Companies.</p>
